    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5eee8a50e296111b124c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Label mappings are the rules you define to tell Grafana how to pull pieces of the Graphite metric path into Loki labels when switching data sources. They are currently only supported between Graphite and Loki queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Graphite data source",
        "Configuration options in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "04a919dc05f03c2f2ea382b7f4ad2c434201bfec",
        "sha256": "f7954b5ab74c873515072b56d4b42ca9ee4ef1e56f0eb6cbc446f48418a66bec",
        "lineStart": 99,
        "lineEnd": 99,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/configure/index.md#L99-L99"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4632e991a89fc8bc66da",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you change your data source from Graphite to Loki, your queries are automatically mapped based on the rules you define. To create a mapping, specify the full path of the metric and replace the nodes you want to map with label names, using parentheses. The corresponding label values are extracted from your Graphite query during the data source switch.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Graphite data source",
        "Configuration options in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "04a919dc05f03c2f2ea382b7f4ad2c434201bfec",
        "sha256": "f7954b5ab74c873515072b56d4b42ca9ee4ef1e56f0eb6cbc446f48418a66bec",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/configure/index.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b31820a9f28cdd4d1c1d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana automatically maps all Graphite tags to labels, even if you haven’t defined explicit mappings. When using matching patterns with `{}`(e.g., `metric.{a,b}.value`), Grafana converts them to Loki’s regular expression matching syntax. If your queries include functions, Graphite extracts the relevant metrics and tags, then matches them against your mappings.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Graphite data source",
        "Configuration options in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "04a919dc05f03c2f2ea382b7f4ad2c434201bfec",
        "sha256": "f7954b5ab74c873515072b56d4b42ca9ee4ef1e56f0eb6cbc446f48418a66bec",
        "lineStart": 103,
        "lineEnd": 103,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/configure/index.md#L103-L103"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
