    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.664c3c94d1453dbbe607",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana lets you reference one query from another using its query letter, similar to how cell references work in a spreadsheet.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Graphite query editor",
        "Nested queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b3c4dd0a3b8fa087860bc7166417b838182a7a0f",
        "sha256": "6ced8f5013d0e7915d51e15ba80ed9f73c86317cb3e7dcc37918a1d2322c61be",
        "lineStart": 110,
        "lineEnd": 110,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md#L110-L110"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ecad008f76485ea85562",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if you add a second query and want to build on the results of query A, you can reference it using #A.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Graphite query editor",
        "Nested queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b3c4dd0a3b8fa087860bc7166417b838182a7a0f",
        "sha256": "6ced8f5013d0e7915d51e15ba80ed9f73c86317cb3e7dcc37918a1d2322c61be",
        "lineStart": 112,
        "lineEnd": 112,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md#L112-L112"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.44f318729fc68f7cb0d8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This approach allows you to build compound or nested queries, making your panels more flexible and easier to manage.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Graphite query editor",
        "Nested queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b3c4dd0a3b8fa087860bc7166417b838182a7a0f",
        "sha256": "6ced8f5013d0e7915d51e15ba80ed9f73c86317cb3e7dcc37918a1d2322c61be",
        "lineStart": 114,
        "lineEnd": 114,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md#L114-L114"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.73eb7fa7ed31f09d12b2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To display multiple time series on the same graph, use wildcards in your query to return all matching series at once.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Graphite query editor",
        "Use wildcards to make fewer queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b3c4dd0a3b8fa087860bc7166417b838182a7a0f",
        "sha256": "6ced8f5013d0e7915d51e15ba80ed9f73c86317cb3e7dcc37918a1d2322c61be",
        "lineStart": 118,
        "lineEnd": 118,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md#L118-L118"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.29425b2e498477f8e1d3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, to monitor CPU utilization across a variety of metrics, you can use a single query like `cpu.percent.*.g` to retrieve all matching time series. This approach is more efficient than writing separate queries for each series, such as `cpu.percent.user.g`, `cpu.percent.system.g`, and others, which would result in multiple queries to the data source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Graphite query editor",
        "Use wildcards to make fewer queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/graphite/query-editor/index.md",
