    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7ea3fea3e33cf38159c8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Brief InfluxDB latency spikes or network interruptions can cause alert rule evaluations to fail. By default, a failed evaluation moves the rule into an error state, which can trigger a large number of spurious notifications at once even though your data is healthy.",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB alerting",
        "Handle transient errors and timeouts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "76e2edca1f14f4c4bc8d5a5073f04c40074b3c49",
        "sha256": "67a61ab6231a24926fd99e9168c2f1c19a2d650afe2daa9ef5fc27a8630de21d",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 130,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/alerting/index.md#L130-L130"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eadd3f0fa7fbd9cb4464",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. In the alert rule settings, expand **Configure no data and error handling** and set **Alert state if execution error or timeout** to **Keep Last State**. The rule keeps its previous state through brief evaluation failures instead of firing an error alert.",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB alerting",
        "Handle transient errors and timeouts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "76e2edca1f14f4c4bc8d5a5073f04c40074b3c49",
        "sha256": "67a61ab6231a24926fd99e9168c2f1c19a2d650afe2daa9ef5fc27a8630de21d",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/alerting/index.md#L134-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.55a6f3808f37c3e22d3a",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. Set a **Pending period** so the alert condition must be met for a sustained period across multiple evaluations before the alert fires.",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB alerting",
        "Handle transient errors and timeouts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/alerting/index.md",
