    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5ecdafe3447b4dd9a8a9",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Timeout** - Sets the HTTP request timeout in seconds. If you don't set a value, Grafana uses the `timeout` setting in the `dataproxy` section of the [configuration file](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#dataproxy), which defaults to `30` seconds. Increase this value if complex queries or large result sets fail with timeout errors such as `context deadline exceeded`. Alert rule evaluations use the same timeout, so increasing it also gives alert queries more time to complete.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the InfluxDB data source",
        "Configuration options",
        "URL and authentication",
        "Advanced HTTP settings"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/configure/_index.md",
