    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.500538e44ff93a47a5d8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you enable the **Multi-value** or **Include all value** options with InfluxQL, Grafana converts the labels from plain text to a regular expression-compatible string, so you must use `=~` instead of `=` and wrap the variable in a regular expression such as `/^$host$/`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB template variables",
        "Choose a variable syntax"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "456916b3c3ccdcf5700d556ce2f5c5e2f7dccd09",
        "sha256": "63605f8531159590ecf2f6daa156138b85929443decbf41c686a992f89d7d747",
        "lineStart": 187,
        "lineEnd": 187,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md#L187-L187"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5f19ed90daebb5572c55",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if `$host` is a multi-value variable and you select `server1` and `server2`, Grafana joins the values with `|`, wraps them in parentheses, and escapes any special characters. The interpolated query looks like this:",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB template variables",
        "Choose a variable syntax"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "456916b3c3ccdcf5700d556ce2f5c5e2f7dccd09",
        "sha256": "63605f8531159590ecf2f6daa156138b85929443decbf41c686a992f89d7d747",
        "lineStart": 189,
        "lineEnd": 189,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md#L189-L189"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a4897cf2a8ae87178188",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you enable the **Multi-value** option with SQL, use the `IN` operator instead of `=` to match multiple values.",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB template variables",
        "Choose a variable syntax"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "456916b3c3ccdcf5700d556ce2f5c5e2f7dccd09",
        "sha256": "63605f8531159590ecf2f6daa156138b85929443decbf41c686a992f89d7d747",
        "lineStart": 205,
        "lineEnd": 205,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md#L205-L205"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.05320190da6adc84f67b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you use a variable inside a regular expression, or when the variable is multi-value, Grafana escapes special characters in the values so the query remains valid. If you need the literal, unmodified value instead, use the `raw` format option:",
      "headingPath": [
        "InfluxDB template variables",
        "Choose a variable syntax",
        "Prevent unwanted value escaping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "456916b3c3ccdcf5700d556ce2f5c5e2f7dccd09",
        "sha256": "63605f8531159590ecf2f6daa156138b85929443decbf41c686a992f89d7d747",
        "lineStart": 209,
        "lineEnd": 209,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/influxdb/template-variables/index.md#L209-L209"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.739b8ac087279dffb639",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This document provides solutions to common issues you may encounter when configuring or using the InfluxDB data source. Issues are organized to follow the typical setup and usage workflow. For configuration instructions, refer to [Configure the InfluxDB data source](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/influxdb/configure/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot InfluxDB data source issues"
      ],
      "source": {
