    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.16040bdfc0bc95c3794b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Loki data source supports [Grafana Alerting](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/). You can alert on your logs so Grafana notifies you when a LogQL metric query crosses a threshold, for example when the rate of error logs spikes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b93226f621e923e571d0f0517b72f178cfd995c",
        "sha256": "5c3a6fa40be98ea9831ca8aab25bc630d2f581ec97907538dde00c638ebbea36",
        "lineStart": 24,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md#L24-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.be4f3db404909f62bd33",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Grafana-managed alert rules:** Grafana evaluates the rule against a LogQL metric query. This is the most common approach and works with any Loki data source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md",
