    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e7c6ab61fba8d8b4bd15",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A Grafana-managed rule evaluates a single number against the threshold. A `range` query returns a time series with many points, which the rule can't evaluate directly. Either set the query **Type** to `instant`, or add a **Reduce** expression, such as **Last** or **Mean**, between the query and the **Threshold** expression. Without one of these, the rule can evaluate incorrectly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki alerting",
        "Best practices",
        "Reduce a time series to a single value"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b93226f621e923e571d0f0517b72f178cfd995c",
        "sha256": "5c3a6fa40be98ea9831ca8aab25bc630d2f581ec97907538dde00c638ebbea36",
        "lineStart": 132,
        "lineEnd": 132,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md#L132-L132"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7f7d803c6957ea5fdb97",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A transient condition, such as a brief network blip or a momentary spike in errors, can cross the threshold for a single evaluation. Set a pending period so the rule fires only after the condition holds for a sustained duration. A pending period of a few evaluation intervals reduces false positives from short-lived conditions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki alerting",
        "Best practices",
        "Set a pending period to avoid false positives"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b93226f621e923e571d0f0517b72f178cfd995c",
        "sha256": "5c3a6fa40be98ea9831ca8aab25bc630d2f581ec97907538dde00c638ebbea36",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7a4418a46e150694c3ef",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A LogQL metric query returns _no series_ when no log lines match, rather than returning a value of `0`. Grafana evaluates a rule that receives no series as **No Data**, not **Normal**, which can cause an alert to enter the No Data state instead of resolving.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki alerting",
        "Best practices",
        "Handle no data versus zero results"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b93226f621e923e571d0f0517b72f178cfd995c",
        "sha256": "5c3a6fa40be98ea9831ca8aab25bc630d2f581ec97907538dde00c638ebbea36",
        "lineStart": 140,
        "lineEnd": 140,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/alerting/index.md#L140-L140"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
