    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0bc434a52e50571ec745",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Annotations](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/build-dashboards/annotate-visualizations/) overlay rich event information on top of graphs. With the Loki data source, annotations are built from log queries: each log line that a LogQL query returns within the dashboard time range becomes an annotation, so you can correlate log events with the rest of your dashboard data.",
