    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a79ebdc5a60b242623e7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use LogQL to wrap a log query with functions that create metrics from your logs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki query editor",
        "Create a metric query"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "fa8cb5cb875450d848fbe24ea8e51347c60f26a8",
        "sha256": "fb91b2da8e977c8a060669eeaffc278336ffb966cb095c2a769e4b29beb50f2e",
        "lineStart": 287,
        "lineEnd": 287,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md#L287-L287"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9bceacf795924f422a87",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Metric queries apply a range aggregation, such as `rate` or `count_over_time`, over a log query and an optional range like `[5m]`. You can then wrap the result in an aggregation operator, such as `sum` or `topk`, to group or rank the series.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki query editor",
        "Create a metric query",
        "Metric query examples"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "fa8cb5cb875450d848fbe24ea8e51347c60f26a8",
        "sha256": "fb91b2da8e977c8a060669eeaffc278336ffb966cb095c2a769e4b29beb50f2e",
        "lineStart": 293,
        "lineEnd": 293,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md#L293-L293"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb948d0bbd36becacf69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Use case: find the noisiest endpoints.** Rank the top 10 request paths by log volume over the last hour:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki query editor",
        "Create a metric query",
        "Metric query examples"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "fa8cb5cb875450d848fbe24ea8e51347c60f26a8",
        "sha256": "fb91b2da8e977c8a060669eeaffc278336ffb966cb095c2a769e4b29beb50f2e",
        "lineStart": 319,
        "lineEnd": 319,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md#L319-L319"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4244af24a609429f7c69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To keep large queries responsive, Grafana automatically splits Loki queries that cover a long time range into a series of smaller sub-queries. Grafana runs the sub-queries and merges the results, and the query progresses incrementally so you see partial results as they arrive. Query splitting applies to both log and metric queries and requires no configuration.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki query editor",
        "Query splitting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "fa8cb5cb875450d848fbe24ea8e51347c60f26a8",
        "sha256": "fb91b2da8e977c8a060669eeaffc278336ffb966cb095c2a769e4b29beb50f2e",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 327,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md#L327-L327"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.68c6b048eaec00c56b4e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Loki stores three types of labels: indexed labels, parsed fields, and structured metadata. The query editor and log details treat all three types as labels you can filter on and use in [derived fields](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/loki/configure/#derived-fields). For more information, refer to the [Loki structured metadata documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/get-started/labels/structured-metadata/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki query editor",
        "Structured metadata"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "fa8cb5cb875450d848fbe24ea8e51347c60f26a8",
        "sha256": "fb91b2da8e977c8a060669eeaffc278336ffb966cb095c2a769e4b29beb50f2e",
        "lineStart": 331,
        "lineEnd": 331,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md#L331-L331"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ae5e97251a8f8b19549c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use Loki log queries as a source for dashboard annotations. For details, refer to [Loki annotations](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/loki/annotations/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki query editor",
        "Apply annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "fa8cb5cb875450d848fbe24ea8e51347c60f26a8",
        "sha256": "fb91b2da8e977c8a060669eeaffc278336ffb966cb095c2a769e4b29beb50f2e",
        "lineStart": 335,
        "lineEnd": 335,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/query-editor/index.md#L335-L335"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a42e918d19a7de26bcb2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Instead of hard-coding details such as server, application, and sensor names in metric queries, you can use variables. Grafana lists these variables in dropdown select boxes at the top of the dashboard to help you change the data displayed in your dashboard. Grafana refers to such variables as template variables.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 25,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L25-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a83756b9187e080372ee",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For an introduction to templating and template variables, refer to the [Templating](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/) and [Add and manage variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/) documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L29-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.aab1e4d5c4a6265b53ec",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Variables of the type _Query_ help you query Loki for lists of labels or label values. The Loki data source provides a form to select the type of values expected for a given variable.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Use query variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
