    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.04dd2b0ca99ba9f515d9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Prefer `$__auto` over `$__range` for the range in a metric query. The `$__range` variable resolves to the entire selected time range, so using it as a range vector, such as `[$__range]`, makes each data point aggregate over the whole window. This can scan far more data and look back further than you intend.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Use the `$__auto` variable for Loki metric queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 112,
        "lineEnd": 112,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L112-L112"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2dc40008800d066b7108",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more information about variables, refer to [Global built-in variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/#global-variables).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Use the `$__auto` variable for Loki metric queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 115,
        "lineEnd": 115,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L115-L115"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2c90915cc1008dc3c2b2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Keep the following limitations in mind when you use template variables with the Loki data source:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 119,
        "lineEnd": 119,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L119-L119"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.825dc2194b73646d8935",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Only indexed labels are available for label variable queries.** A _Query_ variable of type **Label values** returns the values of indexed stream labels. Values that exist only as parsed fields or [structured metadata](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/get-started/labels/structured-metadata/) aren't available, because the variable query doesn't run a log pipeline to extract them.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 121,
        "lineEnd": 121,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L121-L121"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.214d895308adb4041030",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Long time ranges can return incomplete values.** Label and label-value variable queries run over the dashboard's selected time range. Over a long range with high log volume, the query can time out or hit the limits configured in Loki and return an incomplete list of values. Narrow the time range, or add a stream selector to the variable query, so it scans less data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Known limitations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 122,
        "lineEnd": 122,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L122-L122"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.644d84d44a20cf2e9ef2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Labels are key to how Loki aggregates and queries logs. Labels are `key-value` pairs that add contextual information to log entries, and Loki uses them to organize, filter, and search log data efficiently.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Label extraction and indexing in Loki"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 126,
        "lineEnd": 126,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L126-L126"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ee32405f31995ef53a30",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When it ingests logs, Loki extracts labels from log lines using regular expressions, so you can define custom patterns that match your log formats. For example, given a log line like the following:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Label extraction and indexing in Loki",
        "Label extraction"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 130,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L130-L130"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4adfd69f39103f3af9e7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can define a regular expression that extracts the log level (`INFO`), IP address (`A.B.C.D`), and endpoint (`/api/data`) as labels. You can then use those labels to filter and aggregate log entries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Label extraction and indexing in Loki",
        "Label extraction"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6b0e655dd680f1cb30a0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Loki indexes the extracted labels. The index maps labels to their log entries, so Loki can retrieve logs by label without scanning the entire dataset. For example, if a `job` label represents the services in your application, Loki indexes each job's logs separately, so you can query a single job quickly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Label extraction and indexing in Loki",
        "Index labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 140,
        "lineEnd": 140,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L140-L140"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8150024305e3aaef5914",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Combine Loki indexed labels with Grafana template variables to build dynamic queries. Use template variables to select and filter logs by labels such as job names, instance IDs, or severity levels, so you can explore and visualize your log data interactively.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Loki template variables",
        "Label extraction and indexing in Loki",
        "Index labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "bb6baccf3a16af879e02b220ff1c17064cb076ad",
        "sha256": "8193ee3d90cd1d5362b211957442b2274d69f01aad93e856b37b83baf82c751e",
        "lineStart": 142,
        "lineEnd": 142,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/template-variables/index.md#L142-L142"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7ccce5c2fbfec08165fe",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This document provides solutions to common issues you might encounter when configuring or using the Loki data source. For configuration instructions, refer to [Configure the Loki data source](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/loki/configure/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot Loki data source issues"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/troubleshooting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dd06b2e05f654d3aab650bede0784bc9d62bf820",
        "sha256": "7bd76452f86f4f95b8ee8d9b91dbc9615da635d778afd53058bd19c3c1cb9bb9",
        "lineStart": 25,
        "lineEnd": 25,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/loki/troubleshooting/index.md#L25-L25"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e8c0b10467ae98826a63",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This guide covers the Loki data source in Grafana, such as connecting to Loki, running queries, and configuring features. It doesn't cover troubleshooting the Loki service itself. For help with a Loki deployment, including ingestion and query performance, refer to [Manage and debug errors](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/operations/troubleshooting/) in the Loki documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot Loki data source issues"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/loki/troubleshooting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dd06b2e05f654d3aab650bede0784bc9d62bf820",
        "sha256": "7bd76452f86f4f95b8ee8d9b91dbc9615da635d778afd53058bd19c3c1cb9bb9",
        "lineStart": 28,
