    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ccaff35fe7538fe27259",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This document provides instructions for configuring the Microsoft SQL Server data source and explains available configuration options. For general information on adding and managing data sources, refer to [Grafana data sources](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/) and [Data source management](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/data-source-management/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b1c02407dcc69dba175a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This page documents the **Microsoft SQL Server data source**, which lets you query an existing SQL Server database and visualize the results in Grafana. This is different from the [Microsoft SQL Server integration](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana-cloud/monitor-infrastructure/integrations/integration-reference/integration-mssql/) (available in Grafana Cloud), which uses Grafana Alloy to collect performance metrics _about_ your SQL Server instance (CPU, memory, connections, and similar). If you want to monitor the health of SQL Server itself, refer to the integration documentation instead.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L29-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3f8e0cc746b8c8d76758",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Grafana permissions:** You must have the `Organization administrator` role to add and configure data sources. Users with the `Editor` or `Viewer` role cannot access the data source configuration form unless granted additional permissions through [RBAC](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/). Organization administrators can also [configure the data source via YAML](#provision-the-data-source) with the Grafana provisioning system.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Before you begin"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
