      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.12293809bb4ac0176438",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| **krb5 config file path** | Specifies the path to the Kerberos configuration file used by the [MIT krb5 package](https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/krb5-1.12/doc/admin/conf_files/krb5_conf.html).                                                       | `/etc/krb5.conf`     |",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Configure the data source in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 188,
        "lineEnd": 188,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L188-L188"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cda42636c6ae53e391ce",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Windows AD (Kerberos) authentication is only available for self-managed Grafana installations. It is not supported in Grafana Cloud. For Grafana Cloud deployments connecting to SQL Server, use SQL Server Authentication or Azure Entra ID.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Configure the data source in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 191,
        "lineEnd": 191,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L191-L191"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "conditional-or-paid-restriction-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7373ae7e7c2d2ba71264",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For Kerberos authentication to succeed, a Service Principal Name (SPN) must be registered for the SQL Server instance that matches the hostname Grafana uses to connect. This is especially important when connecting through Availability Group Listeners or DNS aliases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Configure the data source in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 196,
        "lineEnd": 196,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L196-L196"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f9498d3caf4497fa971a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If Grafana connects through a Listener or alias, register an additional SPN for that name. Verify registered SPNs with `setspn -L <DOMAIN>\\<SERVICE_ACCOUNT>`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Configure the data source in the UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 205,
        "lineEnd": 205,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L205-L205"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7fae4e43368f138588cd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If your SQL Server instance is in a private network (on-premises, VPN, or VPC), Grafana Cloud cannot reach it directly over the internet. You must use **Private data source connect (PDC)** to establish a secure tunnel between your Grafana Cloud stack and your private network.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Configure the data source in the UI",
        "Connect to on-premises SQL Server from Grafana Cloud"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
        "lineStart": 211,
        "lineEnd": 211,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md#L211-L211"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source > Configure the data source in the UI > Connect to on-premises SQL Server from Grafana Cloud"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.99a267f7ff8c22daaa0b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "PDC is required for any SQL Server that isn't publicly accessible from the internet. Firewall allowlisting alone is not sufficient because Grafana Cloud doesn't use static IP addresses for data source connections.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure the Microsoft SQL Server data source",
        "Configure the data source in the UI",
        "Connect to on-premises SQL Server from Grafana Cloud"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/configure/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "468ac6d022bd91271e046308509eabab23316d3c",
        "sha256": "78f3473345c7acf1680b5e482fdc29c61c6d73576e857090bae5239629ed0887",
