    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e1912fd1fcec531974f8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can enable macro support in the `SELECT` clause to simplify time series query creation. Use the **Data operations** drop-down to choose a macro such as `$\\_\\_timeGroup` or `$\\_\\_timeGroupAlias`, then select a time column from the Column drop-down and a time interval from the Interval drop-down. This generates a time-series query based on your selected time grouping.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server query editor",
        "Time series queries"
