    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ac37f79293c57b26d6ca",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Instead of hard-coding details such as server, application, and sensor names in metric queries, you can use variables. Grafana displays these variables in drop-down select boxes at the top of the dashboard to help you change the data displayed in your dashboard. Grafana refers to such variables as **template variables**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 27,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L27-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ea28f23978bf59f815d6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For general information on using variables in Grafana, refer to [Add variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.708b8e0a0d728e24b605",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For an introduction to templating and template variables, refer to [Templating](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/) and [Add and manage variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 33,
        "lineEnd": 33,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L33-L33"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d14fa40c6a113974cf5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A query variable in Grafana dynamically retrieves values from your data source using a query. With a query variable, you can write a SQL query that returns values such as measurement names, key names, or key values that are shown in a drop-down select box.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b5b42918eae0cd7d1e4c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, the following query returns all values from the `hostname` column:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6b0d8e636e71560f8d2c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A query can return multiple columns, and Grafana automatically generates a list using the values from those columns. For example, the following query returns values from both the `hostname` and `hostname2` columns, which are included in the variable's drop-down list.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 45,
        "lineEnd": 45,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L45-L45"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8669d5d22f48c39c48e0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also create a key/value variable using a query that returns two columns named `__text` and `__value`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a61f620cbab95a3d0a37",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- The `__text` column defines the label shown in the drop-down.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d2aed5f36386222bb46a",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- The `__value` column defines the value passed to panel queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 55,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L55-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a3c9b2b5314b95d103c8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This is useful when you want to display a user-friendly label (like a hostname) but use a different underlying value (like an ID).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 57,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L57-L57"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3953835424c0840e0c21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Note that the values in the `_text` column should be unique. If there are duplicates, Grafana uses only the first matching entry.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 59,
        "lineEnd": 59,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L59-L59"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.36c4003d2e9ae1ac3b1f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also create nested variables, where one variable depends on the value of another. For example, if you have a variable named `region`, you can configure a `hosts` variable to only show hosts from the selected region. If `region` is a multi-value variable, use the `IN` operator instead of `=` to match against multiple selected values.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.989dfd804ae059f00061",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana automatically quotes template variable values only when the template variable is a `multi-value`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4ea7d6363212f57604e4d29ba05a2d571c833ef6",
        "sha256": "443ead52d051116a1045f23c7efa4c7495a5beee835bab7fcc48bf49e213a183",
        "lineStart": 73,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md#L73-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.00f837b8287bcf45d87f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When using a multi-value variable, use the `IN` comparison operator instead of `=` to match against multiple values.",
