      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f425a9fb806be505903e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When the user selects \"All\", `hostname` resolves to `%`, and the `LIKE '%'` matches all rows. When a specific value is selected, `LIKE 'server01'` matches only that value.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Handle the \"All\" option in SQL queries",
        "Pattern: Use a custom \"All\" value with `LIKE`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
