    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9131401b3c9e773f66f0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For `IN` clauses where `%` doesn't work, use a conditional approach. Set the **Custom all value** to `ALL`, then write:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Microsoft SQL Server template variables",
        "Handle the \"All\" option in SQL queries",
        "Pattern: Conditional `WHERE` clause with \"All\""
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/template-variables/index.md",
