    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7b67b08841ca53b2da60",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Cause:** Since Grafana v11.3, multi-value variables used with `IN` are automatically quoted. If you manually wrapped the variable in quotes (for example, `WHERE col IN ('${var}')`), values are now double-quoted (for example, `''value''`), causing query failures.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot Microsoft SQL Server data source issues",
        "Template variable errors",
        "Double-quoting breaks queries with multi-value variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mssql/troubleshooting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "857fcfbb0fbe81ba5933bb2248c97d5e976c3234",
        "sha256": "e521406635abf05194b4cf1322459a1f6d7fda247e573b15a67ae141145589e2",
        "lineStart": 495,
        "lineEnd": 495,
