    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bd63ad1f00ebfcf179e7",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Filter by column value** - _Optional_ If you toggle **Filter** you can add a column to filter by from the drop-down. To filter on more columns, click the **+ sign** to the right of the condition drop-down. You can choose a variety of operators from the drop-down next to the condition. When multiple filters are added you can add an `AND` operator to display all true conditions or an `OR` operator to display any true conditions. Use the second drop-down to choose a filter. To remove a filter, click the `X` button next to that filter's drop-down. After selecting a date type column, you can choose **Macros** from the operators list and select `timeFilter`, which adds the `$\\_\\_timeFilter` macro to the query with the selected date column.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL query editor",
        "MySQL Builder mode"
      ],
      "source": {
