    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.855077c5ed8260b66733",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| `$__time(dateColumn)`                                 | Replaces the value with an expression to convert to a UNIX timestamp and renames the column to `time_sec`. It also helps to recognize the `time` column, as required in Time Series format. Example: _UNIX_TIMESTAMP(dateColumn) AS time_sec_. |",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL query editor",
        "Macros"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "337ba0971e35a147687cf26c4fbdfca2d0957e12",
        "sha256": "72419911caa4b30f1d8ca7cd56d58b2003ddcafbcc4e7f730eecabb535398ee3",
