    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.07ef836348c402213a85",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Instead of hard-coding values like server, application, or sensor names in your metric queries, you can use variables. Variables appear as drop-down select boxes at the top of the dashboard, making it easy to change the data displayed in your dashboard.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL query editor",
        "Template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "337ba0971e35a147687cf26c4fbdfca2d0957e12",
        "sha256": "72419911caa4b30f1d8ca7cd56d58b2003ddcafbcc4e7f730eecabb535398ee3",
        "lineStart": 256,
        "lineEnd": 256,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md#L256-L256"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7cb1958369bd95ca783c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Annotations allow you to overlay event information on your graphs, helping you correlate events with metrics. You can write SQL queries that return event data to display as annotations on your dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL query editor",
        "Annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "337ba0971e35a147687cf26c4fbdfca2d0957e12",
        "sha256": "72419911caa4b30f1d8ca7cd56d58b2003ddcafbcc4e7f730eecabb535398ee3",
        "lineStart": 262,
        "lineEnd": 262,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md#L262-L262"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.84e74f0cab7edfbd992b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use time series queries to create Grafana-managed alert rules. Table formatted queries are not supported in alert rule conditions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL query editor",
        "Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "337ba0971e35a147687cf26c4fbdfca2d0957e12",
        "sha256": "72419911caa4b30f1d8ca7cd56d58b2003ddcafbcc4e7f730eecabb535398ee3",
        "lineStart": 268,
        "lineEnd": 268,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/query-editor/_index.md#L268-L268"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4444442227e9596df0a2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Instead of hard-coding details such as server, application, and sensor names in metric queries, you can use variables. Grafana displays these variables in drop-down select boxes at the top of the dashboard to help you change the data displayed in your dashboard. Grafana refers to such variables as **template variables**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8b4e9af927fd60ebb0f752a26f1b5318eb25a81f",
        "sha256": "782e0b5075e4a5b068515118097fb27d9b7924eba557b77b504f55d9b64978c9",
        "lineStart": 22,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md#L22-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9aaae6c5e07e7bbbf078",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For an introduction to templating and template variables, refer to [Templating](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/) and [Add and manage variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL template variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8b4e9af927fd60ebb0f752a26f1b5318eb25a81f",
        "sha256": "782e0b5075e4a5b068515118097fb27d9b7924eba557b77b504f55d9b64978c9",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ab4b3b736cf0574413e9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A query variable in Grafana dynamically retrieves values from your data source using a query. With a query variable, you can write a SQL query that returns values such as measurement names, key names, or key values that are shown in a drop-down select box.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8b4e9af927fd60ebb0f752a26f1b5318eb25a81f",
        "sha256": "782e0b5075e4a5b068515118097fb27d9b7924eba557b77b504f55d9b64978c9",
        "lineStart": 30,
        "lineEnd": 30,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md#L30-L30"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.02f68e0f044c5686eb62",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The variable query editor supports the same **Builder** and **Code** modes as the main query editor. Use Builder mode to construct queries visually by selecting a dataset, table, columns, and filters. Use Code mode to write SQL directly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "MySQL template variables",
        "Query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8b4e9af927fd60ebb0f752a26f1b5318eb25a81f",
        "sha256": "782e0b5075e4a5b068515118097fb27d9b7924eba557b77b504f55d9b64978c9",
        "lineStart": 32,
        "lineEnd": 32,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/mysql/template-variables/index.md#L32-L32"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8bcd316fdf73fb57ac25",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, the following query returns all values from the `hostname` column:",
