    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.028896f45702440dadd8",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Keep queries fast:** Alert rules evaluate on a schedule (for example, every minute). Avoid expensive joins, subqueries, or scanning large tables without indexes. Add indexes on time columns and any columns used in `WHERE` clauses.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL alerting",
        "Best practices"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "901b418010d37d6488c9b8189d172db15cfd8caa",
        "sha256": "54576f24d747c6a7566681dd39a95cfd676a14e67cb11d23ba513ebcff4e6f6b",
        "lineStart": 121,
        "lineEnd": 121,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/alerting/index.md#L121-L121"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6d26695cd4e851e58ecb",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Use `$__timeFilter`:** Always include a `$__timeFilter` or `$__unixEpochFilter` macro to limit data to the evaluation window. Without it, the query scans the entire table on every evaluation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL alerting",
        "Best practices"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "901b418010d37d6488c9b8189d172db15cfd8caa",
        "sha256": "54576f24d747c6a7566681dd39a95cfd676a14e67cb11d23ba513ebcff4e6f6b",
        "lineStart": 122,
        "lineEnd": 122,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/alerting/index.md#L122-L122"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d159f058b2df29a7b627",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Handle `NULL` values:** If your data contains `NULL` values, Grafana treats them as \"no data.\" Configure the alert rule's **No data** behavior to match your expectations (for example, **Alerting**, **No data**, or **OK**).",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL alerting",
        "Best practices"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "901b418010d37d6488c9b8189d172db15cfd8caa",
        "sha256": "54576f24d747c6a7566681dd39a95cfd676a14e67cb11d23ba513ebcff4e6f6b",
