      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b4a142b241153f27251a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To run a time series query you must include a column named `time` that returns either a SQL `datetime` value or a numeric datatype representing the UNIX epoch time in seconds. Additionally, the query results must be sorted by the `time` column for proper visualization in panels.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 175,
        "lineEnd": 175,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L175-L175"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b0798fc08d6b90f4c00f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Time series query results are returned in [wide data frame format](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/data-frames#wide-format). In the data frame query result, any column, except for time or string-type columns, transforms into value fields. String columns become field labels.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 192,
        "lineEnd": 192,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L192-L192"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4f12cc67cea17e113047",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For backward compatibility, an exception to this rule applies to queries that return three columns, one of which is a string column named `metric`. Instead of converting the metric column into field labels, it's used as the field name, while the series name is set to its value. Refer to the following example.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Metric column detection"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 199,
        "lineEnd": 199,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L199-L199"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f3613d0966c0378af1bf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When using `$__timeGroup` or `$__unixEpochGroup` with a fill parameter (the third argument), Grafana fills gaps in your time series data. This is useful when your data has irregular intervals or missing data points. Fill only works with time series format queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Fill missing time series points"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 204,
        "lineEnd": 204,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L204-L204"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.74ce2274b731cfb48d41",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| Fill mode           | Behavior                                                                              |",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Fill missing time series points"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 208,
        "lineEnd": 208,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L208-L208"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ad5309a930b5696155bf",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| `0` (or any number) | Missing points are filled with the specified numeric value.                           |",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Fill missing time series points"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 210,
        "lineEnd": 210,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L210-L210"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.08f6ae8d515e2752e033",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| `NULL`              | Missing points are filled with `NULL`, which creates gaps in line charts.             |",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Fill missing time series points"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 211,
        "lineEnd": 211,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L211-L211"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c2477e87f842a0d8e020",
      "syntaxRole": "table-row",
      "sourceText": "| `previous`          | Missing points use the last known value. If no previous value exists, `NULL` is used. |",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Fill missing time series points"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 212,
        "lineEnd": 212,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L212-L212"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6f55b47b52c14671147e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As of Grafana 13.0, fill mode in `$__timeGroup` and `$__unixEpochGroup` includes additional safeguards to prevent incorrect data points when the query returns no rows or the time range falls outside the data boundaries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Fill missing time series points"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 217,
        "lineEnd": 217,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L217-L217"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1828a5c32691746d45df",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana applies a server-side row limit to query results to protect against excessive memory usage. If your query returns more rows than the limit, the result is truncated. To reduce the number of rows returned, narrow the dashboard time range, increase the `$__timeGroup` interval, or add a `LIMIT` clause to your query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 222,
        "lineEnd": 222,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L222-L222"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.38bd1971c0182dbe8905",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To customize default series name formatting, refer to [Standard options definitions](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/panels-visualizations/configure-standard-options/#display-name).",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 250,
        "lineEnd": 250,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L250-L250"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c72764a7f0c4a2faf010",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Following are time series query examples.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 252,
        "lineEnd": 252,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L252-L252"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.08b5de59446021d0038d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To return raw time and value points without grouping, use `$__time` to alias your date/time column as `time`:",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 256,
        "lineEnd": 256,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L256-L256"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.23829fd30ff11009c5fb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Based on the data frame result in the following example, the time series panel generates two series named _value 10.0.1.1_ and _value 10.0.1.2_. To display the series names as _10.0.1.1_ and _10.0.1.2_, use the [Standard options definitions](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/panels-visualizations/configure-standard-options/#display-name) display value `${__field.labels.hostname}`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 281,
        "lineEnd": 281,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L281-L281"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b9db5b505b266d9b3296",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When your time column stores UNIX epoch (seconds), use `$__timeEpoch` to alias it as `time` and `$__unixEpochFilter` in the WHERE clause:",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 324,
        "lineEnd": 324,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L324-L324"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a970d77a20bbe453be14",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For grouped time series with epoch columns, use `$__unixEpochGroupAlias` and `$__unixEpochFilter`. Refer to the [Macros](#macros) table for details.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "Time series queries",
        "Row limits"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 335,
        "lineEnd": 335,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L335-L335"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.92b36a2e69e1866220bb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can run `EXPLAIN` and `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` queries in Code mode to inspect query execution plans. The results are returned as a table, which is useful for diagnosing slow queries directly within Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "EXPLAIN queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "da418c753c9813f78e1d4eed64e0946e46a50b3e",
        "sha256": "039487ccd5bee34210f2a93dfc270b66e758127ff361f491daa43c2203030f7f",
        "lineStart": 339,
        "lineEnd": 339,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/query-editor/_index.md#L339-L339"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a99cab5e0ad38cf7e815",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana macros are expanded before the query runs, so you can use `$__timeFilter` and other macros in your `EXPLAIN` queries to see the actual execution plan for the dashboard's time range. Set the **Format** to **Table** to display the plan output.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL query editor",
        "EXPLAIN queries"
      ],
      "source": {
