      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.98ec5b1ae4584a91161f",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Type: Custom** – In **Custom options** > **JSON**, paste your own JSON array with the mapping. Each object in the array can have any number of properties; use `text` and `value` for the label and value shown in the drop-down, and add additional properties as needed. For the JSON format and examples, refer to [Multi-property custom variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/#multi-property-custom-variables) in Add and manage variables.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Multi-property variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 135,
        "lineEnd": 135,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L135-L135"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fceaddd1700a53cf0a5e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Type: Query** – Write a SQL query that returns multiple columns. In the variable editor, set **Value field** and **Text field** to the columns that supply the value and the label for the drop-down. Add one column per property you want to reference; each column name becomes a property name. In panels and queries, reference a property with `${varName.columnName}`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Multi-property variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 137,
        "lineEnd": 137,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L137-L137"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff7ca4db2cdafc1d5dfa",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Example (Type: Query):** A variable named `env` that lists environments with different identifiers per cloud. In the variable editor, set **Text field** to `name` and **Value field** to `id`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Multi-property variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 139,
        "lineEnd": 139,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L139-L139"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6bfb1fb55de06619cbd0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In a panel query you might use `$env.env_aws` for an AWS-related query and `$env.env_azure` for an Azure-related query. For more on the concept, refer to [Configure multi-property variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/#configure-multi-property-variables) in [Add and manage variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Multi-property variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 150,
        "lineEnd": 150,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L150-L150"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c81c60c98032f3e3c37",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana automatically quotes template variable values only when the template variable is a **multi-value** variable.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 154,
        "lineEnd": 154,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L154-L154"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1de41790c5679ad7b782",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When using a multi-value variable, use the `IN` comparison operator instead of `=` to match against multiple values.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
