    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3727e184f15932a05094",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **`[[varname]]` syntax**",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 173,
        "lineEnd": 173,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L173-L173"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b28bc3a8adba9bc0b807",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When a variable has **Multi-value** enabled, Grafana automatically adds quotes around each selected value. For example, if the user selects `web01` and `web02`, `$hostname` expands to `'web01','web02'`. Use the `IN` operator to match:",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries",
        "Multi-value variable with IN clause"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 188,
        "lineEnd": 188,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L188-L188"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.200a02fe648798cac16d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If only a single value is selected, the `IN` clause still works correctly—`IN('web01')` is equivalent to `= 'web01'`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries",
        "Multi-value variable with IN clause"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 201,
        "lineEnd": 201,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L201-L201"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e31e0101298d540a1c3a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For numeric columns (such as IDs), disable quoting with the `csv` format option so values aren't wrapped in quotes:",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries",
        "Multi-value variable with numeric columns"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 205,
        "lineEnd": 205,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L205-L205"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f88fd6bc68815c6da162",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If `host_id` has values `1`, `2`, and `3` selected, this expands to `IN(1,2,3)` instead of `IN('1','2','3')`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries",
        "Multi-value variable with numeric columns"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 211,
        "lineEnd": 211,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L211-L211"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9b93682fa4db5513d612",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, Grafana formats multi-value variables as a quoted, comma-separated string. For example, if `server01` and `server02` are selected, the result is `'server01','server02'`. To disable quoting, use the `csv` formatting option:",
      "headingPath": [
        "PostgreSQL template variables",
        "Use variables in queries",
        "Disable quoting for multi-value variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e6e64d6c3ed9d36f0d02cd77e1fe05e47046e60a",
        "sha256": "bb19076da8c2b9241d06f526cf27f5585c6d69fb5d74dff31d957443108ed5df",
        "lineStart": 215,
        "lineEnd": 215,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/postgres/template-variables/index.md#L215-L215"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
