    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7fc04bf28df9cbfcaf45",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When using OAuth-authenticated Prometheus endpoints (Google Managed Prometheus, Azure Managed Prometheus), queries may succeed in Explore and dashboards but fail intermittently during alert evaluation. This happens because the alerting backend handles token refresh differently from the interactive query path.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus alerting",
        "Limitations",
        "OAuth token handling differs between Explore and Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e69dbca4761d655d38dedb0f31723b55544cc771",
        "sha256": "9fbd02d532e4f3f69b6a33cf37499ff66969256513cda97768e0be208e052bad",
        "lineStart": 250,
        "lineEnd": 250,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md#L250-L250"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c72cc8465d6d4a88654c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you're using GCP, consider the **datasource-syncer** pattern, a sidecar process that refreshes OAuth tokens and updates the data source credentials on a schedule shorter than the token lifetime.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus alerting",
        "Limitations",
        "OAuth token handling differs between Explore and Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e69dbca4761d655d38dedb0f31723b55544cc771",
        "sha256": "9fbd02d532e4f3f69b6a33cf37499ff66969256513cda97768e0be208e052bad",
        "lineStart": 252,
        "lineEnd": 252,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md#L252-L252"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb8d84c6c61923ff8354",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana can display Prometheus alerting rules but can't create or modify them through the UI. To manage Prometheus-native alerting rules, edit your Prometheus rule files directly and reload the configuration.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus alerting",
        "Limitations",
        "Data source-managed rules are read-only"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e69dbca4761d655d38dedb0f31723b55544cc771",
        "sha256": "9fbd02d532e4f3f69b6a33cf37499ff66969256513cda97768e0be208e052bad",
        "lineStart": 258,
        "lineEnd": 258,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md#L258-L258"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2b5c8c1c74e158ae8b21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, when a Grafana-managed alert rule encounters an execution error or timeout (such as a network blip, i/o timeout, or a transient 502 from Prometheus), the rule enters an **Error** state, which fires the alert. This can cause false alarms and spam on-call teams when the underlying issue is a brief connectivity interruption rather than a genuine threshold breach.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus alerting",
        "Configure alert state for execution errors"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e69dbca4761d655d38dedb0f31723b55544cc771",
        "sha256": "9fbd02d532e4f3f69b6a33cf37499ff66969256513cda97768e0be208e052bad",
        "lineStart": 262,
        "lineEnd": 262,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md#L262-L262"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d3ad8fba4fbcfaf27098",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To prevent false positives from transient errors, configure the **Alert state if execution error or timeout** setting on each alert rule:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus alerting",
        "Configure alert state for execution errors"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/alerting/index.md",
