    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.31b2967571788d4320c3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If your queries hit memory or sample limits, refer to [Memory limit exceeded for high-cardinality queries](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/prometheus/troubleshooting/#memory-limit-exceeded-for-high-cardinality-queries).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus query editor",
        "Query high-cardinality data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cdc563c3108dcd9de35912dff1febc0228715bda",
        "sha256": "dc2247aa971e1b7926cb68555c77d8874fd592b3a2d6c533b9124b98204dc690",
        "lineStart": 310,
        "lineEnd": 310,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md#L310-L310"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a76e73f61c942bfafab0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This is expected. If you need integer results, wrap the expression in `ceil()` or `floor()`:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus query editor",
        "Expected PromQL behaviors",
        "`increase()` returns fractional values on integer counters"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cdc563c3108dcd9de35912dff1febc0228715bda",
        "sha256": "dc2247aa971e1b7926cb68555c77d8874fd592b3a2d6c533b9124b98204dc690",
        "lineStart": 320,
        "lineEnd": 320,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md#L320-L320"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7d929ad069ab52cc1a1c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If `rate()` shows an ever-increasing value instead of a steady per-second rate, the most common cause is multiple instances writing to the same time series without unique distinguishing labels. Prometheus merges these into a single series with an artificially growing counter.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus query editor",
        "Expected PromQL behaviors",
        "`rate()` appears to grow over time"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cdc563c3108dcd9de35912dff1febc0228715bda",
        "sha256": "dc2247aa971e1b7926cb68555c77d8874fd592b3a2d6c533b9124b98204dc690",
        "lineStart": 328,
        "lineEnd": 328,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md#L328-L328"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e7b4cf58873c22ce2306",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you see this after a deployment or scaling event, verify your service discovery is assigning unique `instance` labels to each target.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus query editor",
        "Expected PromQL behaviors",
        "`rate()` appears to grow over time"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "cdc563c3108dcd9de35912dff1febc0228715bda",
        "sha256": "dc2247aa971e1b7926cb68555c77d8874fd592b3a2d6c533b9124b98204dc690",
        "lineStart": 336,
        "lineEnd": 336,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/query-editor/_index.md#L336-L336"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb895f39dee8c38f98af",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When a monitored process restarts, its counters reset to zero. Prometheus handles this with counter reset detection: `rate()` and `increase()` account for resets and don't produce negative values. However, you may still see a brief spike at the reset point because the first scrape after a restart reports the full counter value accumulated since the restart.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Prometheus query editor",
        "Expected PromQL behaviors",
        "Counter reset spikes after pod restarts"
      ],
      "source": {
