    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ab4ac934d0b4a098a20c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Cause:** The Grafana alerting backend and the interactive query path (Explore, dashboards) handle credential refreshes differently. The alerting evaluator can use a cached OAuth token beyond its expiry window due to a token staleness check issue in the Prometheus data source. This causes alerting to fail with expired credentials while interactive queries succeed because they trigger a fresh token exchange.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot Prometheus data source issues",
        "Authentication errors",
        "OAuth token expiration errors (GCP and Azure)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/troubleshooting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "8e50ee5b80f0d882f5c254bfa20a82f2a9d1c982",
        "sha256": "5d62682b47e6f29d1a4603953a8584079c2b939a9feca62c15b80a8307623e18",
        "lineStart": 163,
