    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f4612d9c6293e5d751ae",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Prometheus annotations create a marker for **every data point** returned by the query. There's no automatic filtering of zero values. If you only want annotations at specific moments, your PromQL expression must return data only at those times (for example, using `> 0`, `changes() > 0`, or the `ALERTS` metric).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot Prometheus data source issues",
        "Annotation errors",
        "Annotations not appearing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/prometheus/troubleshooting/index.md",
