    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.64b0dc17e3e2bb2537af",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Clicking **Logs for this span** filters by trace ID, not span ID, so results include all logs for the entire trace that contain a matching trace ID, not only logs emitted during that specific span. If your results look broader than expected, this is expected behavior. To narrow results to a specific span's activity, write a custom LogQL query that filters on span ID or span-specific attributes if your application logs them, for example `{service_name=\"my-service\"} | json | spanId=\"\"`. For this feature to work at all, your application must inject trace IDs into log lines, for example, using OpenTelemetry SDK structured logging. Without trace IDs in logs, the query falls back to a time-range filter.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure trace to logs correlation",
        "Configure the Tempo data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-logs.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "79b27dac6a84e3f457842a932b3a17ddb32c8024",
