    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.73d3018073fbf0755161",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. Select **Save and Test**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure trace to metrics correlation",
        "Set up a basic configuration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3a874f96d0fd6bc3d0ed6847f9cf1e6fda46c416",
        "sha256": "07a34143f831f7b56fc90f88ad40803b34f7d385a85ec30be2c12ba376c15cae",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ccbdb3405c8be21d9e75",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To use custom queries, you need to configure the tags you'd like to include in the linked queries. For each tag, the key is the span attribute name. In cases where the attribute name would result in an invalid metrics query or doesn't exactly match the desired label name, you can enter the label name as the second value. For example, you could map the attribute `k8s.pod` to the label `pod`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure trace to metrics correlation",
        "Set up custom queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3a874f96d0fd6bc3d0ed6847f9cf1e6fda46c416",
        "sha256": "07a34143f831f7b56fc90f88ad40803b34f7d385a85ec30be2c12ba376c15cae",
        "lineStart": 69,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md#L69-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.09c5d56261f240934b08",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can interpolate the configured tags using the `$__tags` keyword. For example, when you configure the query `requests_total{$__tags}` with the tags `k8s.pod=pod` and `cluster`, it results in `requests_total{pod=\"nginx-554b9\", cluster=\"us-east-1\"}`. The label values are dynamically inserted based on the span attributes' values.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure trace to metrics correlation",
        "Set up custom queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3a874f96d0fd6bc3d0ed6847f9cf1e6fda46c416",
        "sha256": "07a34143f831f7b56fc90f88ad40803b34f7d385a85ec30be2c12ba376c15cae",
        "lineStart": 74,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md#L74-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.75eaf63a6cc3bc63cdaf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can link to any metric you'd like, but metrics for span durations, counts, and errors filtered by service or span are a great starting point.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure trace to metrics correlation",
        "Set up custom queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/configure-trace-to-metrics.md",
