    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a8187bd9f61c3ce2626c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this query, `service_name` is the only [stream label](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/get-started/labels/) used inside `{}`. Stream labels should be low-cardinality values that describe the source of your logs. The `trace_id` field appears after the `|` pipe as a [pipeline filter](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/query/log_queries/#line-filter-expression), which searches log content or [structured metadata](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/get-started/labels/structured-metadata/) without creating additional streams. Don't use trace IDs or other high-cardinality values as stream labels because each unique value creates a separate stream, which degrades Loki performance. For more information, refer to [Label best practices](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/get-started/labels/bp-labels/) and [Cardinality](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/get-started/labels/cardinality/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Trace correlations",
        "Examples",
        "Example 1: Trace to logs by service name and trace identifier"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/trace-correlations.md",
