    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6c6a67ac30174c215686",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. The Service Graph view table uses a different set of metrics from the node graph. The Grafana frontend queries `traces_spanmetrics_calls_total` and `traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket`. Confirm that these metrics exist in your linked Prometheus data source. Newer Tempo versions may produce `traces_spanmetrics_duration_seconds_bucket` instead of `traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket`. If you only have the newer metric name, the duration column shows no data until the Grafana frontend supports the renamed metric.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Troubleshoot Tempo data source issues",
        "Service graph issues",
        "Service Graph view table is empty"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/datasources/tempo/troubleshooting/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "39a0f51bf9a95c054012e8ed995cf2c0797a1612",
